-- S2 wave · Category 9 (Compliance & Legal) — seed 9 platform baseline skills into paige_skills.
--
-- Run through the generic S1b interpreter (default dispatch) — NO bespoke handler. category = 'compliance_legal'
-- (canonical §15, locked by the CHECK in 20260830000000). IP-CLEAN per §14/§62 (mechanic-descriptive only — no
-- anchor-person name, no branded legal-framework/product title, no source-repo name). tier_availability = §61
-- default; scoping = 'platform'.
--
-- §13 "NOT LEGAL ADVICE" GUARD (the KEY gate for this category): EVERY skill carries an EXPLICIT in-copy
-- disclaimer — in BOTH the description AND a step — that the output is a generic starting template / general
-- information, NOT legal, tax, or regulatory advice; Paige is not a lawyer and makes no legal determination; the
-- tenant must have it reviewed by a qualified attorney/professional for their jurisdiction before relying on it.
-- compliance_requirement_scan (the ONE read) carries the HEAVIEST guard and NEVER asserts the tenant is or is not
-- compliant. (crew advice_disclaimer_ok=true.)
--
-- §13 INTERPRETER-HONEST: 1 read_only+auto (compliance_requirement_scan — surfaces general considerations to
-- research, persists nothing, "not available / consult a professional" fallback, no legal conclusion) + 8
-- DRAFTERS (draft+confirm, file a draft for approval). NONE publish, file with an authority, submit, send, or
-- determine legal/compliance status.
--
-- §2 FINANCE-CLEAN (platform default): coaching-generic business governance ONLY (privacy, terms, refund,
-- consent, recordkeeping, disclaimers, contract-review checklist) — ZERO consumer-finance wording. The §1
-- verifier CAUGHT + SCRUBBED 2 banned-token hits that lived inside a disclaimer/guard (refund_policy_draft's
-- anchor said "financing"; compliance_requirement_scan's guard named a "regulated-lending vertical") and
-- rephrased them positively ("not legal, tax, or regulatory advice"); the shipped set is §2-clean (the §32.a
-- proof's finance scan re-verifies 0 hits).
--
-- §18 EXCLUSIONS (wrap-don't-duplicate): these are business-wide GOVERNANCE artifacts, distinct from Cat 2
-- draft_engagement_contract (the negotiated client CONTRACT itself) and draft_sop_process_doc (an operational
-- SOP), and from Cat 7 HR/people-management docs. contract_review_checklist is a PRE-SIGNING review checklist
-- (what to look for), NOT the contract. privacy_policy_draft (external published policy) vs
-- data_handling_summary_draft (internal overview of the business's own practices) differ by audience/purpose.
--
-- SOURCING LINEAGE (attribution here in the reference ONLY, never in a row, per §14): Anthropic Skills registry
-- structure + standard small-business governance mechanics (plain-language privacy/ToS/refund/consent/
-- recordkeeping/disclaimer drafting, generic compliance-consideration surfacing, pre-signing contract-review
-- checklist) — mechanics only, IP-clean, no branded legal product.
--
-- §1 crew: 2 distillation engineers + adversarial IP/§16/§18/§2/§13-not-advice verifier. Verdict FIX_NEEDED
--   because the verifier caught + scrubbed the 2 §2 disclaimer/guard hits above and confirmed all 9 carry the
--   NOT-LEGAL-ADVICE disclaimer (advice_disclaimer_ok=true); the corrected set is §2/§13-clean.
-- ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING makes this idempotent + safe to re-run.

