    $j$[{"id": "read_declared_business", "tool": "context", "desc": "Read ONLY the tenant's DECLARED business type and region from tenant context — never assume or infer a vertical the tenant did not declare (§38 vendor/assumption-clean). Where the declared type or region is missing, note it as 'not available' rather than guessing."}, {"id": "gather_general_considerations", "tool": "rag", "desc": "Retrieve GENERAL, coaching-generic compliance-consideration topics that a client-based service business commonly researches (privacy notices, client consent, recordkeeping, plain-language disclosures) — as neutral areas-to-look-into keyed to the declared business/region, never as legal conclusions or jurisdiction-specific requirements."}, {"id": "compose_considerations_with_hard_guard", "tool": "anthropic", "desc": "Compose the general considerations as a list of topics the tenant MAY want to look into, in the tenant's voice (§3), under a HEAVY, explicit NOT-LEGAL-ADVICE / NOT-A-VERDICT guard: state up front and reinforce that this is general information only, NOT legal, tax, or regulatory advice; that Paige is not a lawyer; that this makes NO determination that the tenant is or is not compliant with anything; and that the tenant should consult a qualified attorney/professional for their jurisdiction. For anything that cannot be known from the declared data, say 'not available — consult a qualified professional', never a conclusion. Coaching-generic only, phrased positively everywhere including the guard ('this is general information, not legal, tax, or regulatory advice'), and never referencing any regulated vertical (§2). Persist NOTHING."}]$j$::jsonb,
    ARRAY[$s$context$s$, $s$rag$s$, $s$anthropic$s$]::text[],
    $s$read_only$s$, $s$auto$s$,
    $s$The ONE read skill of the compliance category — read_only + auto, persists nothing (NO client_memory, NO pdf_render step) so it never files a draft or record (§16). Distinct from the Cat 2 documents and Cat 7 HR docs (§18): it does not draft any artifact; it only surfaces general governance topics to research. Mechanic: read declared business type + region, retrieve general coaching-generic compliance-consideration topics, compose them under a heavy NOT-LEGAL-ADVICE / NOT-A-COMPLIANCE-VERDICT guard with explicit 'not available / consult a professional' fallbacks. The §13 not-advice guard is the KEY gate here and is deliberately the heaviest: the skill NEVER asserts the tenant is or is not compliant and NEVER states a jurisdiction-specific legal requirement as fact. IP-clean: no branded framework, anchor person, or source-repo name (§14/§62). Interpreter honesty: it reports general considerations grounded in declared data and says 'not available' where it cannot know — it cannot determine legal or compliance status (§13).$s$,
