    $s$draft$s$, $s$confirm$s$,
    $s$Gather-then-generate review-checklist mechanic: assemble the tenant's declared business/region context, retrieve generic contract-review consideration categories, and synthesize a plain-language pre-signing checklist of what to look for — then file it as a draft for human approval. §18 scope: this is a REVIEW CHECKLIST (things to examine before signing), NOT the Cat 2 draft_engagement_contract skill (which drafts the actual client agreement) and NOT the operational draft_sop_process_doc; it is a compliance/governance aid, not the legal instrument itself. §13 gate: every output carries an in-copy NOT-LEGAL-ADVICE disclaimer (general template, consult a qualified attorney, Paige makes no legal determination). The interpreter only gathers context and persists a draft — it cannot review authoritatively, sign, or determine legal sufficiency. IP-clean: no branded framework, anchor person, or source-repo name (§14/§62).$s$,
